What is advisory Locking ?

	- Locks are not forced by the OS 
	- All processes must cooperate 
	- Used to protect critical section in files 

Locking Commands 

	F_GETLK  :- Check if lock exists
	
	F_SETLK  :- Set / release lock (non-blocking)

	F_SETLKW :- Set lock (wait if unavailable)


Lock Types 

	F_RDLCK 	// Read Lock 
	F_WRLCK		// Write Lock
	F_UNLCK		// Unlock 


Struct flock 

	struct flock {
	    
	    short l_type;     // F_RDLCK, F_WRLCK, F_UNLCK
	    short l_whence;   // SEEK_SET, SEEK_CUR, SEEK_END
	    off_t l_start;    // Starting offset
	    off_t l_len;      // Number of bytes to lock
	    pid_t l_pid;      // PID (used with F_GETLK)
	};


Region Locking Example 

	v.l_start = 10;
	v.l_len   = 5;

	Bytes 10 to 15 are locked 

	|---------|XXXXXXXX|---------|
	          10      15


Locking flow 


	P1  --->  lock file region  --->  write data  ---> unlock
	P2  --->  waits for lock    --->  write data


Why F_SETLKW is used ?

	if lock is available -> acquired immediately 
	if not available     -> process waits 

	prevents race conditions in file access 










































